<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ Sept yr current account deficit NZ$4.2 bln.</title>
<headline>NZ Sept yr current account deficit NZ$4.2 bln.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Monday released the following balance of payments data for the September 1996 quarter and the year to September.</p>
<p>Rounded actual figures, in millions of NZ dollars (- is deficit). &quot;Revised from&quot; figures are in brackets.</p>
<p>		    Sept 1996 qtr     June 1996 qtr    Sept 1995 qtr</p>
<p>Merch trade	  -317		  +752 (+740)	  -202</p>
<p>Invisibles	   -1854		 -1631 (-1576)	-1447</p>
<p>Balance		-2171		 -861 (-836)	  -1649</p>
<p>	  Sept year current account data</p>
<p>		     Yr-Sept 1996     Yr-June 1996	Yr-Sept 1995</p>
<p>Merch trade	    625		740 (728)	   1583</p>
<p>Invisibles	   -4828	    -4422 (-4385)	-5508</p>
<p>Balance		-4203	    -3681 (-3657)	-3924</p>
<p>SNZ said the deficit was 4.6 percent of GDP at Sept 30 vs 4.1 percent at June 30.</p>
<p>Note - economists forecast a quarterly account deficit of $1.71 billion and an annual deficit of $3.71 billion.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473 4746</p>
